---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { ArrowRight, ArrowUpRight } from "@lucide/astro";
import { repositoryUrl } from "../lib/content";
---
<SiteLayout title="Local-first privacy · Rastry" description="Rastry processes images locally, without accounts, uploads, or telemetry enabled by default." breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Rastry", path: "/" }, { name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy/" }]}>
  <div class="article-shell">
    <header><p class="kicker">Trust</p><h1>Files stay where the work happens.</h1><p class="article-shell__summary">Rastry is designed as a local-first tool. This is a plain-language description of the current product behavior, not a promise about unshipped services.</p></header>
    <article class="article">
      <h2>No image uploads</h2>
      <p>The CLI and Desktop workflow process image bytes on the user's machine. The public website is documentation only; it has no image upload or browser editor.</p>
      <h2>No account required</h2>
      <p>Current workflows do not require sign-in, cloud storage, or a remote image-processing account.</p>
      <h2>Telemetry is off by default</h2>
      <p>The repository does not enable analytics or telemetry by default. Any future opt-in measurement must be explicit, documented, and privacy-preserving.</p>
      <h2>What the site does</h2>
      <p>This static site serves HTML, CSS, fonts, SVG brand assets, and a local release feed. It does not send submitted image files anywhere because it does not accept them.</p>
      <p>For implementation details, see the <a class="icon-link" href={repositoryUrl + "/blob/main/rastry.md"} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">product definition <ArrowUpRight size={14} /></a> and <a class="icon-link" href="/docs/safety/">safety documentation <ArrowRight size={14} /></a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
